            "review_title": "Review at Nhà Hàng Kim's",
            "review_text": "impartialspectator\nSydney, Australia778 contributions\n0\nSolid, better than 3, no 4\nJan 2025 • Couples\nThe place was on a list of dining recommendations our hotel (on Ly Tu Trong, a parallel street) provided. We checked the (three) reviews and decided to take the risk. Had local beer, the spring rolls with crab meat, and the fried rice with crab meat and prawns. Decent but by no means overwhelming. Kim's is really a run-down hole in the wall; the state of the menus is telling. \n\nThe bill was odd. We were given some unspecified 5% discount, on top of which was levelled a 5% \"service charge\" (a first we have encountered in Vietnam) and on top of that an 8% VAT charge was added. In the end it is just a few Aussie dollars, but I prefer things like service charges (and VAT) revealed on the menu.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten January 15, 2025",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
